---
const states = [
  ['Active insights','Newly generated insights appear as active. Operators can filter and sort by severity, type, device and pillar before deciding what deserves attention.'],
  ['Resolved automatically','Some insights expire or resolve when their threshold condition ends. The system marks the resolution source and keeps the event in history for audit and compliance.'],
  ['Information only','Advisory signals—such as an end-of-life date still two years away—remain visible without inflating urgent counts. Useful context, minus the manufactured panic.'],
];
const actions = [
  ['Snooze or defer','Set an hour, day, week or custom period. The insight reactivates automatically and remains identifiable through a snoozed filter.'],
  ['Dismiss','Remove an invalid, false-positive or already-tracked insight from the active count, with justification and stronger confirmation for critical findings.'],
  ['Retrieve or reinstate','Review dismissed history, filter by dismissal reason and restore one or many insights when the operating context changes.'],
  ['Acknowledge','Record that an insight has been seen without presenting it as unresolved dashboard work.'],
];
const decisions = [
  ['False positive / buggy insight','Allow reporting as a false positive, send useful telemetry for product improvement and preserve the event in dismissed or reported history.'],
  ['Bulk actions','Select multiple insights, then dismiss, snooze or change state without turning repetitive administration into a lifestyle.'],
  ['Audit trail','Log every state change—active, snoozed, dismissed and restored—so compliance reviews and incident post-mortems can answer who changed what and why.'],
  ['Role-specific controls','Apply persona guardrails: administrators can snooze operational issues, operations leaders can dismiss appropriate findings, and high-severity security actions remain restricted.'],
];
const images = [
  ['agentic-insight-vertical-title.png','Exploration 01','A vertical title treatment tested hierarchy against a dense operational canvas.'],
  ['agentic-insight-horizontal-title.png','Exploration 02','The horizontal treatment increased scan speed and left more room for insight evidence.'],
  ['agentic-insight-revisit.png','Revisited direction','The structure was simplified after reviewing balance, hierarchy and action visibility.'],
  ['agentic-insight-visual-balance.png','Visual balance','Device health, insight distribution and priority were tuned as one composition.'],
  ['agentic-insight-pillar.png','Pillar view','A pillar-led view tested whether operators could orient by operational domain.'],
  ['agentic-insight-pillar-device.png','Pillar + device','The combined model connected system-level patterns with device-level evidence.'],
  ['agentic-insight-device.png','Device view','A device-first variation supported operators who begin with known infrastructure.'],
  ['agentic-insight-empty.png','No-insights state','The empty state explains system health without rewarding the dashboard for simply being quiet.'],
  ['agentic-insight-filtered.png','Filtered state','Applied filters keep the active question visible while narrowing the evidence set.'],
];
---

<div class="insight-journey">
  <header class="insight-hero">
    <a href="/work/agenticops#agentic-trust">← Back to Trust journey</a>
    <p>Journey 01 · Insight page</p>
    <h1>Before an agent can act, the signal has to make sense.</h1>
    <div><p>The first journey establishes the trust foundation: help an operator understand what changed, decide whether it matters and control what happens next.</p><aside>Phase 01 · AI Ops<br/><b>Understanding before automation</b></aside></div>
  </header>

  <nav aria-label="Insight journey chapters"><a href="#exploration">Exploration</a><a href="#states">Insight states</a><a href="#actions">Insight actions</a><a href="#decisions">Phase 2 decisions</a><a href="#settings">Settings</a></nav>

  <section id="exploration" class="journey-section exploration">
    <p class="index">01 / Design exploration</p><h2>Finding the right hierarchy before polishing the dashboard.</h2>
    <p class="lead">The exploration tested title direction, information density, device-versus-pillar orientation and the balance between system health and actionable insight. Each screen below is an exact artifact exported from the Figma board.</p>
    <div class="artifact-grid">{images.map(([file,label,caption],index) => <figure class:list={{wide:index>1}}><div><img src={`/images/agentic-insight/${file}`} alt={`${label}: AgenticOps Insight Page design exploration`} loading={index>1?'lazy':'eager'} /></div><figcaption><span>{label}</span><p>{caption}</p></figcaption></figure>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section id="states" class="journey-section dark-section">
    <p class="index">02 / Insight states</p><h2>Not every signal deserves the same urgency—or the same shelf life.</h2>
    <div class="state-grid">{states.map(([title,copy],index) => <article><span>{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section id="actions" class="journey-section">
    <p class="index">03 / Insight actions</p><h2>Give operators a useful vocabulary between “fix now” and “ignore forever.”</h2>
    <div class="action-grid">{actions.map(([title,copy],index) => <article><span>{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></div></article>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section id="decisions" class="journey-section decision-section">
    <p class="index">04 / Needed decisions in Phase 2</p><h2>Agentic action introduced four decisions the interface could not politely avoid.</h2>
    <div class="decision-grid">{decisions.map(([title,copy]) => <article><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></article>)}</div>
  </section>

  <section id="settings" class="journey-section settings-section">
    <p class="index">05 / Settings</p><h2>Governance belongs in the journey—not in a forgotten admin drawer.</h2>
    <div class="settings-card"><div><span>Dismissal reason</span><b>Mandatory or optional</b><p>Require a reason such as false positive, acknowledged or not relevant.</p></div><div><span>Dismissal duration</span><b>Permanent or temporary</b><p>Allow automatic reset after a defined number of days.</p></div><div><span>Automatic restoration</span><b>When the anomaly returns</b><p>Restore a dismissed insight if the same condition recurs within the chosen window.</p></div><div><span>Dismissal scope</span><b>Device or global</b><p>Apply the choice only to one device—or consistently across matching devices.</p></div></div>
    <a class="back-card" href="/work/agenticops#agentic-trust"><span><small>Journey complete</small><strong>Return to the five connected journeys</strong></span><b>Back to Trust journey →</b></a>
  </section>
</div>

